Guest thunk libraries hand out host function pointers (vkGetInstanceProcAddr)
linked to invokers inside them. A dlclose unmaps the invokers but the link
stays, and a later dlopen maps them elsewhere without relinking: the guest
jumps into freed memory. Chromium closes its Vulkan loader after probing it,
then Zink opens it again. Guest thunks are now never unloaded.

--- a/ThunkLibs/GuestLibs/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ThunkLibs/GuestLibs/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -188,6 +188,10 @@
   target_link_options(${NAME}-guest PRIVATE "LINKER:-soname,${SONAME}")
   set_target_properties(${NAME}-guest PROPERTIES NO_SONAME ON)
 
+  # Never unloaded: the host function pointers they hand out stay linked to their invokers (AddThunkTrampolineIRHandler)
+  # after a dlclose, and a later dlopen would map the invokers elsewhere.
+  target_link_options(${NAME}-guest PRIVATE "LINKER:-z,nodelete")
+
   if (GENERATE_GUEST_INSTALL_TARGETS)
     if (BITNESS EQUAL 64)
       install(TARGETS ${NAME}-guest DESTINATION
